Most likely he was summoned by another demon - and this was most
likely the result of you meeting a Chameleon (shape-changing monster):
chameleons look like other monsters, and even have the powers of the
other monsters they change into, but change shape every few seconds.
So, if it turns into a demon, it could summon another demon which
stands a small chance of being a demon lord, if it turns into a giant
it can pick up boulders, or if it turns into a yellow light it could
explode and die.

(Other shape-changing monsters are "doppelgangers", who can turn into
any random @, and "sandestins", who can turn into any of a selection
of nasty monsters and never turn into wimps. Having the intrinsic of
"protection from shape changers", usually gotten by wearing a ring of
this power, forces all shape-changers to appear in their otherwise
seldom-seen natural form, and all were-creatures to appear in human
form so they cannot bite you and give you lycanthropy.

Alternatively, sacrificing YOUR OWN race on an altar will summon a
demon lord - hostile if you are non-chaotic, peaceful (but not tame)
if you are chaotic. It will also turn the altar chaotic, whether you
are chaotic or not, and anger your god if you are not chaotic.

Juiblex is a demon lord who you should meet later in the dungeon - he
has his own dungeon level. However, if you meet him earlier (and kill
him or leave him behind on a level), you won't meet him then, his
level will just be full of his minions - mostly oozes, slimes and
jellies.

